MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Step Back and Goin' Home feel like natural next choices because their blues guitar connects with what interests me in Clapton and Hendrix; Step Back is the album I would choose today.",
    "Hypnotic Eye and The Black Crowes fit the guitar-driven rock side of my interests, while High Hopes and Standing in the Breach also appeal through their songwriting."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The River & The Thread and Wallflower miss today's focus: country-oriented songwriting and vocal-focused performances are less appealing to me right now than blues guitar.",
    "Morning Phase feels too subdued for this visit, and Chicago's Now does not draw me toward the blues and guitar-driven sound I want."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to assume that interest in established musicians means I want a broad selection of their newer albums, even when the sound differs from what I want today.",
    "My interest in songwriting seems to carry too much weight when it leads to albums without the blues guitar emphasis that makes Step Back especially appealing."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between Old Sock and People, Hell & Angels matters especially through expressive blues guitar, which is my strongest interest on this visit.",
    "An album can fit my taste without being something I would choose now: I would save Goin' Home for later, and the live format makes the Black Crowes release less appealing today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in experienced rock and blues musicians, but only some capture today's preference for expressive blues guitar."
}
